      "body": "## Overview\n\nOn a 2-NUMA CPU host, DP=2 × TP=2 assigns device ids `[2, 3]` to DP rank 1. Those ids were filtered as NUMA nodes, the visible-node list became empty, and `CPUWorker` raised `IndexError` on `[0]`. Fixes #64497.\n\n## Claims\n\n- `get_visible_memory_node([2, 3])` returns the real visible nodes `[0, 1]` when neither id is a NUMA node.\n- An assigned id that is a real node is still honored (`[1, 4]` on nodes `{0, 1}` stays `[1]`).\n\n## Validation\n\n`python3 -m pytest tests/utils_/test_cpu_resource_utils.py::test_visible_memory_node_falls_back_when_device_ids_are_not_numa_nodes tests/utils_/test_cpu_resource_utils.py::test_visible_memory_node_assigned_ids_are_limited_to_allowed_nodes -q --noconftest`\n\nBefore the fallback the new test got `[]`. After it, both tests passed. No GPU.\n\n## Details\n\n`assigned_physical_gpu_ids` is a device-rank block, not a NUMA node list, once TP > 1. If none of those ids exist as memory nodes, keep the process-visible node list instead of returning empty.",
